[1m[38;5;10mmalloc_usable_size[0m is not an allocation-size oracle.[22m It produced two convincing-looking "divergences" (72 vs 88 bytes; 1052656 vs 1048600) with byte-identical contents. glibc reuses binned chunks, hands a chunk over whole when the remainder is too small to split, and self-tunes its mmap threshold after large frees — so the value tracks heap state, not the request. [38;5;10mmallopt[0m and warm-up allocations both failed to fix it (glibc's [38;5;10mcalloc[0m bypasses tcache).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
